# Cloudflare Pages header pinning.
# One global rule: every file must revalidate with the server before reuse.
# This is a no-build static site, so a cached script can leave the site
# running a mix of old and new code - correctness beats a few extra
# conditional requests, and Cloudflare ETags make revalidation cheap (304s).
# NOTE: a zone-level Browser Cache TTL (e.g. 4h) can override this header
# for cacheable types (.js/.css). If curl -I shows max-age=14400 on /app.js
# again, set Browser Cache TTL to 'Respect Existing Headers' in the dashboard.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
